{"user": "why did that h1 move flip the WHOLE top row like that, i wasnt expecting 6 discs to go at once", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T23:02:57.502073+00:00", "assistant": "Because **h1 bracketed the entire top row horizontally**.\n\nOthello flips work like this: when Black plays a disc, look in each straight direction. If there\u2019s a chain of White discs ending in a Black disc, **all White discs in between flip**.\n\nSo before that move, the top row must have looked like:\n\n**a1 = Black**, **b1\u2013g1 = White**, **h1 = empty**\n\nWhen Black played **h1**, the row became:\n\n**Black at h1 \u2014 White discs g1 through b1 \u2014 Black at a1**\n\nThat\u2019s a complete bracket, so **b1\u2013g1 all flipped at once**. Six discs in one line is legal.\n\nFinal board count here: **Black 41, White 23** \u2014 Black wins.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T23:02:57.502073+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T23:03:02.502073+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 1, "General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 0.3333333333333333, "General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Bo